From 03681958487bf2c6177ec3b81505d38d9a2c6a91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Luo <u8076655@anu.edu.au>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:50:22 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] List-grouped residual refinement for the global two-stage
 search

After the global primary top-T, refinement groups the T candidates by IVF list (a counting sort
over a small open-addressing map, O(T + nprobe), no sort of the candidates), opens each list once
-- one set_list, one ScopedCodes, one ScopedIds -- and refines its candidates together, optionally
in ascending offset. Refined distances and ids are kept at each candidate's position and pushed
into the result heap in primary order, so results, including ties, are bit-identical to the
one-at-a-time loop, which stays as the fallback and as refine_grouping = 0. Both entry points
(search_preassigned and the rotated-query path) share the implementation. Scratch is thread_local
and reused across queries.

IndexIVFJHQ::refine_grouping (-1 auto, 0 original, 1 grouped, 2 grouped + ascending offset) and
refine_grouping_min_candidates select the path; IndexIVFJHQStats gains the counters (two-stage
queries, candidates, lists opened, set_list calls, scoped acquisitions, grouped queries, primary
and refinement time, scratch bytes). Not stored in the index file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
